IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g6-nouns`
IMPORT `g6-schedule-three`
IMPORT `g6-notice-and-hearing`

-- g6-amount.l4: ss.45-47.  The addition for a continuing violation (s.45(a)) and for a repeat violation
-- (s.45(b)), the floor (s.46), the day on which the amount is updated (s.47(a)), the yearly update by the
-- consumer price index with rounding to NIS 10 (s.47(b)), and the Commissioner's duty to publish the updated
-- amounts (s.47(c)).
--
-- Money is in new shekels.  The base of every calculation is the Third Schedule's column B amount
-- (g6-schedule-three), which is a named refusal at a dash.
--
-- Periods owned here (PLAN section (d)):
--   P28, s.45(a): "one fiftieth for each month in which the violation continues".  A count of months, kind V,
--     not a deadline; IL s.10(b) says what a month after an event is, and is used for the count.  The reading
--     of "each month in which the violation continues" is fork F-MONTHS: months completed (taken), or calendar
--     months touched, with or without the first.  IL s.10(c) is not applied (kind V, ruling 4).
--   P29, s.45(b): "within two years of the previous violation": kind B in the lead's assignment note (a
--     classification window, not a time for doing something): IL s.10 does not speak of "within" (NOTES F8).
--     The calendar arithmetic is IL s.10(b)'s end rule (the same-numbered day, or the month's last day), the
--     only rule the sources give for "two years after a day"; IL s.10(c) is NOT applied; the reading that applies
--     it (the PLAN's kind W) is callable.  The last day is inside the window.
--   P30, s.47(b): "each 1 January": kind R, a recurring date, outside IL s.10 (it is not a period).
--
-- Not in the sources: the first update day (the Law says the amounts are updated each 1 January, and does not
-- say from which one); the tie when a rounded amount is exactly half-way between two multiples of NIS 10;
-- whether the additions of s.45 are themselves rounded; whether the fiftieth is of the fixed amount as enacted
-- or as updated; the rates of reduction under s.46(b) (no regulations are in the sources).

§ `Chapter 6: administrative enforcement measures`

§§ `Subchapter A: imposing a financial sanction`

§§§ `ss 45 to 47: the acts`

@desc The acts of ss.45 to 47: imposing a sanction below the amounts fixed (forbidden, s.46(a)), prescribing the circumstances for lower amounts (s.46(b)) and publishing the updated amounts in Reshumot (s.47(c)); the first field says who performs each act
DECLARE `Act under ss 45 to 47` IS ONE OF
    `impose a financial sanction in this amount`
        HAS `performed by the sanctioning officer` IS A Party
            `the amount imposed` IS A NUMBER
    `prescribe by regulations the circumstances and rates for lower amounts`
        HAS `performed by the regulation-making Minister` IS A Party
    `publish in Reshumot a notice of the updated amounts of the financial sanction`
        HAS `performed by the publishing officer` IS A Party

§§§ `s 45(a): a continuing violation, one fiftieth of the fixed sanction for each month`

-- src:365 | {{ח:סעיף|45|הפרה נמשכת והפרה חוזרת}}
-- src:366 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} בהפרה נמשכת ייווסף על העיצום הכספי הקבוע לאותה הפרה החלק החמישים שלו לכל חודש שבו נמשכת ההפרה.
-- The fixed sanction is "the financial sanction fixed for that violation": the column B amount.  Whether it is
-- the amount as enacted or as updated by s.47(b) is fork F-BASE; the amount is a plain input here and the
-- composition below takes the updated amount (the reading taken).
--
-- "each month in which the violation continues": F-MONTHS.  Three counts, each callable:
--   * the months COMPLETED: month k ends on the last day of a period of k months after the day the violation
--     started (IL s.10(b)), and counts only if the violation was still continuing on that last day.  This is the
--     reading taken: it is the narrower, and a sanction is read strictly against the person it burdens.
--   * the calendar months TOUCHED, first and last (part) months included.
--   * the calendar months touched after the first (the first month being the month of the violation itself,
--     for which the fixed sanction is the sanction).
-- The violation starts on `start` and last continued on `end`; both are inputs.
@ref s.45(a) (src:366)
GIVEN start IS A DATE
      end IS A DATE
      k IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 45(a) — the months completed from` start `to` end `, counting on from month` k MEANS
    IF   `s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` k `months after an event on` start AT MOST end
    THEN 1 PLUS (`s 45(a) — the months completed from` start `to` end `, counting on from month` (k PLUS 1))
    ELSE 0

@ref s.45(a) (src:366)
@export The number of whole months a violation continued, each month ending on the same-numbered day after the day the violation started (Interpretation Law s.10(b)) and counting only if the violation was still continuing on that day
GIVEN start IS A DATE @desc The day the violation started, as an ISO 8601 date
      end IS A DATE @desc The last day the violation continued, as an ISO 8601 date
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 45(a) — the whole months a violation continued from` start `to` end MEANS
    `s 45(a) — the months completed from` start `to` end `, counting on from month` 1

@ref s.45(a) (src:366)
GIVEN start IS A DATE
      end IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 45(a) — the calendar months touched by a violation from` start `to` end MEANS
    IF   end LESS THAN start
    THEN 0
    ELSE (((DATE_YEAR end) TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH end)) MINUS (((DATE_YEAR start) TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH start)) PLUS 1

@ref s.45(a) (src:366)
GIVEN start IS A DATE
      end IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 45(a) — the calendar months touched after the first, by a violation from` start `to` end MEANS
    max 0 ((`s 45(a) — the calendar months touched by a violation from` start `to` end) MINUS 1)

-- "the fiftieth part of it for each month": amount / 50 for each of the months.
@ref s.45(a) (src:366)
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
      months IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 45(a) — the addition of one fiftieth of` amount `for each of the months` months MEANS
    (amount DIVIDED BY 50) TIMES months

§§§ `s 45(b): a repeat violation, an amount equal to the fixed sanction`

-- src:367 | {{ח:תת|(ב)}} בהפרה חוזרת ייווסף על העיצום הכספי הקבוע לאותה הפרה סכום השווה לעיצום הכספי כאמור; לעניין זה, ”הפרה חוזרת“ – הפרת הוראה מההוראות לפי חוק זה כאמור {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 41|בסעיף 41}}, בתוך שנתיים מההפרה הקודמת של אותה הוראה שבשלה הוטל על המפר עיצום כספי או שבשלה הורשע.
-- "a repeat violation: breach of a provision of this Law as stated in s.41, within two years of the previous
-- violation of the same provision for which a sanction was imposed on the violator or for which he was
-- convicted".
-- The anchor is the DATE OF THE PREVIOUS VIOLATION (its act), qualified by its having ended in a sanction or a
-- conviction (the relative clause).  P29, kind B: the window is two years after that day, IL s.10(b)'s end
-- rule, and IL s.10(c) is not applied.
@ref s.45(b) (src:367)
GIVEN previous IS A `Previous violation`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 45(b) — the last day of the two years from the previous violation` previous MEANS
    `s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 2 `years after an event on` (previous's `date of the act`)

-- The reading that applies IL s.10(c) to the window (the PLAN's kind W).
@ref s.45(b) (src:367)
GIVEN previous IS A `Previous violation`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 45(b) — the last day of the two years from the previous violation, when s 10(c) applies` previous calendar MEANS
    `s 10(b), (c) — the last day of a period of` 2 `years after an event on` (previous's `date of the act`) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`Chapter 6 — the days of rest, recess or holiday of` calendar)

-- "the same provision": the provision column A names (items (1) and (2) both s.3(a); items (5) and (6) both
-- s.18(a)).  F-SAME: the alternative takes the same Third Schedule ITEM.
@ref s.45(b) (src:367)
GIVEN previous IS A `Previous violation`
      violation IS A Violation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45(b) — the previous violation` previous `was of the same provision as` violation MEANS
    `Third Schedule — the provision contravened by` (previous's `the listed violation`) EQUALS `Third Schedule — the provision contravened by` (violation's `the listed violation`)

@ref s.45(b) (src:367)
GIVEN previous IS A `Previous violation`
      violation IS A Violation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45(b) — the previous violation` previous `was of the same Third Schedule item as` violation MEANS
    previous's `the listed violation` EQUALS violation's `the listed violation`

-- A previous violation makes this one a repeat violation when: it is the same violator's; it is of the same
-- provision; a sanction was imposed for it or the violator was convicted; it came before this one; and this one
-- is within the two years (the last day inside).
@ref s.45(b) (src:367)
GIVEN violation IS A Violation
      previous IS A `Previous violation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45(b) — the previous violation makes the violation a repeat violation` violation previous MEANS
        "the same violator" ... previous's `the violator`'s `reference for the person` EQUALS violation's `the violator`'s `reference for the person`
    ... "of the same provision" ... `s 45(b) — the previous violation` previous `was of the same provision as` violation
    ... "a sanction was imposed or the violator was convicted" ... (previous's `a financial sanction was imposed for it` OR previous's `the violator was convicted for it`)
    ... "the previous violation came first" ... previous's `date of the act` LESS THAN violation's `date of the act`
    AND "within two years" ... violation's `date of the act` AT MOST `s 45(b) — the last day of the two years from the previous violation` previous

@ref s.45(b) (src:367)
@export Whether a violation is a repeat violation under s.45(b): the same violator, the same provision, a sanction imposed or a conviction for the previous violation, and the violation within two years after the previous one
GIVEN violation IS A Violation @desc One act that breached a listed provision: who committed it (an individual or a corporation), which Third Schedule item it breached, the act's reference and its day
      `the violator's previous violations` IS A LIST OF `Previous violation` @desc The violator's earlier violations, each with its item, its day, and whether a sanction was imposed or a conviction obtained
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45(b) — the violation` violation `is a repeat violation, given` `the violator's previous violations` MEANS
    any (GIVEN previous YIELD `s 45(b) — the previous violation makes the violation a repeat violation` violation previous) `the violator's previous violations`

-- The alternatives: the same Third Schedule item (F-SAME), and s.10(c) applied to the window (F-WINDOW).
@ref s.45(b) (src:367)
GIVEN violation IS A Violation
      previous IS A `Previous violation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45(b) — the previous violation, read by Third Schedule item, makes the violation a repeat violation` violation previous MEANS
        previous's `the violator`'s `reference for the person` EQUALS violation's `the violator`'s `reference for the person`
    AND `s 45(b) — the previous violation` previous `was of the same Third Schedule item as` violation
    AND (previous's `a financial sanction was imposed for it` OR previous's `the violator was convicted for it`)
    AND previous's `date of the act` LESS THAN violation's `date of the act`
    AND violation's `date of the act` AT MOST `s 45(b) — the last day of the two years from the previous violation` previous

@ref s.45(b) (src:367)
GIVEN violation IS A Violation
      previous IS A `Previous violation`
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45(b) — the previous violation, with s 10(c) applied to the window, makes the violation a repeat violation` violation previous calendar MEANS
        previous's `the violator`'s `reference for the person` EQUALS violation's `the violator`'s `reference for the person`
    AND `s 45(b) — the previous violation` previous `was of the same provision as` violation
    AND (previous's `a financial sanction was imposed for it` OR previous's `the violator was convicted for it`)
    AND previous's `date of the act` LESS THAN violation's `date of the act`
    AND violation's `date of the act` AT MOST `s 45(b) — the last day of the two years from the previous violation, when s 10(c) applies` previous calendar

-- "an amount equal to the said financial sanction is added": the fixed sanction again.
@ref s.45(b) (src:367)
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
      `the violation is a repeat violation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 45(b) — the addition for a repeat violation of` amount `where` `the violation is a repeat violation` MEANS
    IF   `the violation is a repeat violation`
    THEN amount
    ELSE 0

§§§ `s 46: the floor, and the power to allow lower amounts`

-- src:369 | {{ח:סעיף|46|סכומים מופחתים}}
-- src:370 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} הממונה אינו רשאי להטיל עיצום כספי בסכום הנמוך מהסכומים הקבועים לפי {{ח:פנימי|פרק ו סימן א|סימן זה}}, אלא לפי הוראות סעיף קטן (ב).
-- src:371 | {{ח:תת|(ב)}} השר, בהסכמת שר המשפטים ובאישור ועדת העבודה והרווחה של הכנסת, רשאי לקבוע נסיבות ושיקולים שבשלהם יהיה ניתן להטיל עיצום כספי בסכום הנמוך מהסכומים הקבועים לפי {{ח:פנימי|פרק ו סימן א|סימן זה}}, ובשיעורים שיקבע.
-- (a): "The Commissioner may not impose a financial sanction in an amount lower than the amounts fixed under
-- this subchapter, except under (b)".  s.45 is in the same subchapter (ss.41 to 51), so "the amounts fixed
-- under this subchapter" are the fixed sanction PLUS the s.45 additions: the floor is the whole sum.
@ref s.46(a) (src:370)
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
      `the amounts fixed under the subchapter` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 46(a) — a sanction of` amount `is not lower than the amounts fixed, which are` `the amounts fixed under the subchapter` MEANS
    amount AT LEAST `the amounts fixed under the subchapter`

-- (b): lower amounts only "in circumstances and considerations, and at rates, that the Minister shall set"
-- by regulations.  No regulation is in the sources (PLAN IP14): so a floor that depends on them is a named
-- refusal unless the caller supplies the rate of reduction those regulations fix (a fraction: 0.2 is a
-- reduction of a fifth).  s.57(a)(4) speaks of "the rates of reduction", which is why the input is a rate of
-- reduction and not a rate payable.
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`s 46(b) — no regulations fixing the circumstances and the rates for lower amounts are in the sources, so no lower floor can be computed` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 46(b) — no regulations fixing the circumstances and the rates for lower amounts are in the sources, so no lower floor can be computed"

@ref s.46(a), s.46(b) (src:370-371)
GIVEN `the amounts fixed under the subchapter` IS A NUMBER
      `the Commissioner relies on circumstances and rates fixed under section 46(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rate of reduction those regulations fix` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 46 — the lowest sanction the Commissioner may impose` `the amounts fixed under the subchapter` `the Commissioner relies on circumstances and rates fixed under section 46(b)` `the rate of reduction those regulations fix` MEANS
    IF   NOT `the Commissioner relies on circumstances and rates fixed under section 46(b)`
    THEN `the amounts fixed under the subchapter`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the rate of reduction those regulations fix`
         WHEN JUST rate THEN `the amounts fixed under the subchapter` TIMES (1 MINUS rate)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 46(b) — no regulations fixing the circumstances and the rates for lower amounts are in the sources, so no lower floor can be computed`

-- (a) as a prohibition: the Commissioner SHANT impose less than the lowest sanction.  The act carries the amount
-- imposed; the guard says when the act is the forbidden one.
@ref s.46(a) (src:370)
GIVEN `the lowest sanction the Commissioner may impose` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under ss 45 to 47`
`s 46(a) — the Commissioner shall not impose a sanction below the floor of` `the lowest sanction the Commissioner may impose` MEANS
    PARTY `the Commissioner`
    SHANT `impose a financial sanction in this amount` `the Commissioner` imposed
          PROVIDED imposed LESS THAN `the lowest sanction the Commissioner may impose`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the Commissioner` BECAUSE "s 46(a): the Commissioner imposed a financial sanction lower than the amounts fixed under the subchapter"

-- (b) is a power of the Minister, with the Minister of Justice's consent and the Committee's approval, over
-- circumstances and rates that are the regulations' content (an input).
@ref s.46(b) (src:371)
GIVEN `the Minister of Justice consented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under ss 45 to 47`
`s 46(b) — the Minister may set the circumstances and rates for lower amounts` `the Minister of Justice consented` `the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the regulations` MEANS
    IF   `the Minister of Justice consented` AND `the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the regulations`
    THEN PARTY `the Minister`
         MAY   `prescribe by regulations the circumstances and rates for lower amounts` `the Minister`
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§§ `s 47(a): the day on which the sanction is updated`

-- src:373 | {{ח:סעיף|47|סכום מעודכן של העיצום הכספי}}
-- src:374 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} העיצום הכספי יהיה לפי סכומו המעודכן ביום מסירת דרישת התשלום, ולגבי מפר שלא טען את טענותיו לפני הממונה כאמור {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 44|בסעיף 44(ד)}} – ביום מסירת ההודעה על כוונת חיוב; הוגש ערעור לבית המשפט לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 56|סעיף 56}} ועוכב תשלומו של העיצום הכספי בידי הממונה או בידי בית המשפט, יהיה העיצום הכספי לפי סכומו המעודכן ביום ההחלטה בערעור.
-- "The sanction shall be at its updated amount on the day the payment demand is delivered; for a violator who did
-- not make representations as in s.44(d), on the day the notice of intention is delivered; if an appeal was filed
-- under s.56 and payment was stayed by the Commissioner or the court, on the day of the decision on the appeal."
-- The three limbs are tried in the order of their strength: the stayed appeal is a proviso that comes last in
-- the sentence and says "shall be ... on the day of the decision", which displaces the other two (fork F-DAY).
-- NOTHING: the appeal has been filed and payment stayed but the court has not yet decided, so the day does not
-- exist yet (a fact about the case, not a gap in the Law).
@ref s.47(a) (src:374)
GIVEN `the day the notice of intention was delivered` IS A DATE
      `representations were made within the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the payment demand is delivered or treated as delivered` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `an appeal was filed and payment was stayed by the Commissioner or the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the decision on the appeal` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 47(a) — the day on which the amount of the sanction is updated` `the day the notice of intention was delivered` `representations were made within the period` `the day the payment demand is delivered or treated as delivered` `an appeal was filed and payment was stayed by the Commissioner or the court` `the day of the decision on the appeal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   `an appeal was filed and payment was stayed by the Commissioner or the court`
        THEN `the day of the decision on the appeal`
        IF   NOT `representations were made within the period`
        THEN JUST `the day the notice of intention was delivered`
        OTHERWISE `the day the payment demand is delivered or treated as delivered`

-- The alternative order (F-DAY): the demand's day first, the stayed appeal only if no demand day is known.
@ref s.47(a) (src:374)
GIVEN `the day the notice of intention was delivered` IS A DATE
      `representations were made within the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the payment demand is delivered or treated as delivered` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `an appeal was filed and payment was stayed by the Commissioner or the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the decision on the appeal` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 47(a) — the day on which the amount of the sanction is updated, the demand's day before the appeal's` `the day the notice of intention was delivered` `representations were made within the period` `the day the payment demand is delivered or treated as delivered` `an appeal was filed and payment was stayed by the Commissioner or the court` `the day of the decision on the appeal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   NOT `representations were made within the period`
        THEN JUST `the day the notice of intention was delivered`
        IF   `an appeal was filed and payment was stayed by the Commissioner or the court`
        THEN `the day of the decision on the appeal`
        OTHERWISE `the day the payment demand is delivered or treated as delivered`

§§§ `s 47(b): the yearly update by the consumer price index, rounded to NIS 10`

-- src:375 | {{ח:תת|(ב)}} סכומי העיצום הכספי הקבועים לפי {{ח:פנימי|פרק ו סימן א|סימן זה}} יתעדכנו ב־1 בינואר בכל שנה (בסעיף קטן זה – יום העדכון), בהתאם לשיעורי שינוי המדד הידוע ביום העדכון לעומת המדד שהיה ידוע ב־1 בינואר של השנה הקודמת; הסכום האמור יעוגל לסכום הקרוב שהוא מכפלה של 10 שקלים חדשים; לעניין זה, ”מדד“ – מדד המחירים לצרכן שמפרסמת הלשכה המרכזית לסטטיסטיקה.
-- "The fixed amounts shall be updated each 1 January (the update day) by the rate of change of the index known
-- on the update day against the index known on 1 January of the previous year; the said amount shall be rounded
-- to the nearest multiple of NIS 10."  The index is the consumer price index the Central Bureau of Statistics
-- publishes: domain.l4's `Price index reading`, with its day of publication; the index "known on" a day is the
-- reading with the latest month among those published by then (a reading published ON the day is known on it).
-- Kind R: each 1 January, a recurring date, not a period.
@ref s.47(b) (src:375)
GIVEN x IS A DATE
      readings IS A LIST OF `Price index reading`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Price index reading`
`s 47(b) — the readings published by` x `among` readings MEANS
    filter (GIVEN reading YIELD reading's `published on` AT MOST x) readings

-- The reading of the latest month in a non-empty list.
@ref s.47(b) (src:375)
GIVEN best IS A `Price index reading`
      rest IS A LIST OF `Price index reading`
GIVETH A `Price index reading`
`s 47(b) — the latest month among` best `and` rest MEANS
    CONSIDER rest
    WHEN EMPTY THEN best
    WHEN other FOLLOWED BY more THEN
        IF   ((other's `year of the index`) TIMES 12) PLUS (other's `month of the index`) GREATER THAN ((best's `year of the index`) TIMES 12) PLUS (best's `month of the index`)
        THEN `s 47(b) — the latest month among` other `and` more
        ELSE `s 47(b) — the latest month among` best `and` more

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`s 47(b) — no reading of the index had been published on that day, so the index known on it is not given` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 47(b) — no reading of the index had been published on that day, so the index known on it is not given"

@ref s.47(b) (src:375)
GIVEN x IS A DATE
      readings IS A LIST OF `Price index reading`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47(b) — the index known on` x `among` readings MEANS
    CONSIDER (`s 47(b) — the readings published by` x `among` readings)
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `s 47(b) — no reading of the index had been published on that day, so the index known on it is not given`
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY more THEN (`s 47(b) — the latest month among` first `and` more)'s `value of the index`

-- "to the nearest multiple of NIS 10": half-way (a multiple of 5 that is not a multiple of 10) is not settled by
-- the Law; the reading taken rounds half UP (F-ROUND); half to even is callable.
@ref s.47(b) (src:375)
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47(b) — the nearest multiple of NIS 10 to` amount MEANS
    (FLOOR ((amount DIVIDED BY 10) PLUS 0.5)) TIMES 10

@ref s.47(b) (src:375)
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47(b) — the nearest multiple of NIS 10, a half going to the even multiple, to` amount MEANS
    (ROUND (amount DIVIDED BY 10)) TIMES 10

-- The amount after the update of 1 January of year y: the amount after the update of the previous year,
-- times the index known on 1 January of y over the index known on 1 January of y-1, rounded.  Before the first
-- update year, the amount is the base.  Each year's rounded amount is the base of the next (F-CHAIN).
@ref s.47(b) (src:375)
GIVEN base IS A NUMBER
      year IS A NUMBER
      `the year of the first update day` IS A NUMBER
      readings IS A LIST OF `Price index reading`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47(b) — the amount of` base `after the update of 1 January of` year `, the first update being in` `the year of the first update day` `and the index readings being` readings MEANS
    IF   year LESS THAN `the year of the first update day`
    THEN base
    ELSE `s 47(b) — the nearest multiple of NIS 10 to` (before TIMES (`index on 1 January` DIVIDED BY `index on 1 January of the year before`))
    WHERE
        before MEANS `s 47(b) — the amount of` base `after the update of 1 January of` (year MINUS 1) `, the first update being in` `the year of the first update day` `and the index readings being` readings
        `index on 1 January` MEANS `s 47(b) — the index known on` (YMD year 1 1) `among` readings
        `index on 1 January of the year before` MEANS `s 47(b) — the index known on` (YMD (year MINUS 1) 1 1) `among` readings

-- The fixed amount as updated on a day: the update of the last 1 January on or before that day.
@ref s.47(b) (src:375)
@export The amount of a fixed sanction in new shekels after the yearly updates by the consumer price index up to a day, each year's result rounded to the nearest NIS 10
GIVEN base IS A NUMBER @desc The amount in new shekels before any update, for example a Third Schedule column B amount
      day IS A DATE @desc The day up to which the amount is updated, as an ISO 8601 date
      `the year of the first update day` IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the first 1 January on which the amounts are updated, for example 2026
      readings IS A LIST OF `Price index reading` @desc The consumer price index readings: each reading's year, month, day of publication and value
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47(b) — the amount of` base `updated on` day `, the first update being in` `the year of the first update day` `and the index readings being` readings MEANS
    `s 47(b) — the amount of` base `after the update of 1 January of` (DATE_YEAR day) `, the first update being in` `the year of the first update day` `and the index readings being` readings

-- The same, rounding a half to the even multiple (F-ROUND) and carrying the unrounded amount from year to year,
-- rounding only at the end (F-CHAIN).  The unrounded chain: the base times each year's ratio.
@ref s.47(b) (src:375)
GIVEN base IS A NUMBER
      year IS A NUMBER
      `the year of the first update day` IS A NUMBER
      readings IS A LIST OF `Price index reading`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47(b) — the unrounded amount of` base `after the update of 1 January of` year `, the first update being in` `the year of the first update day` `and the index readings being` readings MEANS
    IF   year LESS THAN `the year of the first update day`
    THEN base
    ELSE before TIMES (`index on 1 January` DIVIDED BY `index on 1 January of the year before`)
    WHERE
        before MEANS `s 47(b) — the unrounded amount of` base `after the update of 1 January of` (year MINUS 1) `, the first update being in` `the year of the first update day` `and the index readings being` readings
        `index on 1 January` MEANS `s 47(b) — the index known on` (YMD year 1 1) `among` readings
        `index on 1 January of the year before` MEANS `s 47(b) — the index known on` (YMD (year MINUS 1) 1 1) `among` readings

@ref s.47(b) (src:375)
GIVEN base IS A NUMBER
      day IS A DATE
      `the year of the first update day` IS A NUMBER
      readings IS A LIST OF `Price index reading`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47(b) — the amount of` base `updated on` day `, rounded once at the end, the first update being in` `the year of the first update day` `and the index readings being` readings MEANS
    `s 47(b) — the nearest multiple of NIS 10 to` (`s 47(b) — the unrounded amount of` base `after the update of 1 January of` (DATE_YEAR day) `, the first update being in` `the year of the first update day` `and the index readings being` readings)

§§§ `ss 45 to 47 together: the financial sanction for a violation`

-- The sanction: the fixed amount, as updated on the s.47(a) day, plus one fiftieth of it for each month of a
-- continuing violation, plus an equal amount for a repeat violation.  The additions are computed on the UPDATED
-- fixed amount and are not themselves rounded (F-BASE, F-ADD).  A dash in column B, or a day on which the index
-- cannot be read, is a refusal returned in return position.
-- Trap T15: the cap of s.41(b) does not bound this amount: item (5) for a corporation (40,000) plus a repeat
-- addition (40,000) is 80,000 before any update, and more after one.
@ref s.41(a), s.45, s.47 (src:366-367, src:374-375)
@export The financial sanction payable for one violation of the Third Schedule: the amount column B fixes, updated by the consumer price index on the s.47(a) day, plus one fiftieth of it for each month of a continuing violation, plus an equal amount for a repeat violation
GIVEN violation IS A Violation @desc One act that breached a listed provision: who committed it (an individual or a corporation), which Third Schedule item it breached, the act's reference and its day
      `the number of months for which the violation continued` IS A NUMBER @desc The whole number of months for which the violation continued, counted as s.45(a) is read in the encoding (see the fork on months); 0 if it is not a continuing violation
      `the violation is a repeat violation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the violation is a repeat violation under s.45(b), or is treated as one under s.54(b)
      `the day on which the amount is updated` IS A DATE @desc The day s.47(a) names as the day the amount is updated, as an ISO 8601 date such as 2027-06-01
      `the year of the first update day` IS A NUMBER @desc The year of the first 1 January on which the Third Schedule amounts are updated, for example 2026
      `the index readings` IS A LIST OF `Price index reading` @desc The consumer price index readings the Central Bureau of Statistics publishes: each reading's year, month, day of publication and value
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation` violation `the number of months for which the violation continued` `the violation is a repeat violation` `the day on which the amount is updated` `the year of the first update day` `the index readings` MEANS
    updated PLUS continuing PLUS repeating
    WHERE
        updated MEANS `s 47(b) — the amount of` (`s 41(a) — the amount the Third Schedule fixes for the violation` violation) `updated on` `the day on which the amount is updated` `, the first update being in` `the year of the first update day` `and the index readings being` `the index readings`
        continuing MEANS `s 45(a) — the addition of one fiftieth of` updated `for each of the months` `the number of months for which the violation continued`
        repeating MEANS `s 45(b) — the addition for a repeat violation of` updated `where` `the violation is a repeat violation`

-- The alternative base (F-BASE): the additions are computed on the amount as enacted, and the total is then
-- updated and rounded once.
@ref s.41(a), s.45, s.47 (src:366-367, src:374-375)
GIVEN violation IS A Violation
      `the number of months for which the violation continued` IS A NUMBER
      `the violation is a repeat violation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the amount is updated` IS A DATE
      `the year of the first update day` IS A NUMBER
      `the index readings` IS A LIST OF `Price index reading`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation, with the additions computed on the amount as enacted` violation `the number of months for which the violation continued` `the violation is a repeat violation` `the day on which the amount is updated` `the year of the first update day` `the index readings` MEANS
    `s 47(b) — the amount of` (enacted PLUS continuing PLUS repeating) `updated on` `the day on which the amount is updated` `, the first update being in` `the year of the first update day` `and the index readings being` `the index readings`
    WHERE
        enacted MEANS `s 41(a) — the amount the Third Schedule fixes for the violation` violation
        continuing MEANS `s 45(a) — the addition of one fiftieth of` enacted `for each of the months` `the number of months for which the violation continued`
        repeating MEANS `s 45(b) — the addition for a repeat violation of` enacted `where` `the violation is a repeat violation`

-- The alternative that the additions are a power and not an automatic charge (fork F-ADD): s.42(b)(4) tells the
-- Commissioner to state in the notice "the authority to add to the amount of the sanction for a continuing or repeat
-- violation, and the rate of the addition", while s.45 says the additions "shall be added" ("yivasef").  The reading
-- taken is s.45's: they are added whenever the violation is continuing or repeat.  Here the Commissioner's decision
-- to add them is an input.
@ref s.42(b)(4), s.45 (src:366-367)
GIVEN violation IS A Violation
      `the number of months for which the violation continued` IS A NUMBER
      `the violation is a repeat violation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner adds the additions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the amount is updated` IS A DATE
      `the year of the first update day` IS A NUMBER
      `the index readings` IS A LIST OF `Price index reading`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation, the additions being at the Commissioner's discretion` violation `the number of months for which the violation continued` `the violation is a repeat violation` `the Commissioner adds the additions` `the day on which the amount is updated` `the year of the first update day` `the index readings` MEANS
    IF   `the Commissioner adds the additions`
    THEN `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation` violation `the number of months for which the violation continued` `the violation is a repeat violation` `the day on which the amount is updated` `the year of the first update day` `the index readings`
    ELSE `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation` violation 0 FALSE `the day on which the amount is updated` `the year of the first update day` `the index readings`

-- The alternative that the cap of s.41(b) also bounds what is payable (fork F-CAP): the sanction held to the cap for the
-- kind of person.  Not the reading taken: s.41(b) speaks of "the amount of the financial sanction that shall be set in
-- column B" by an order, not of what is payable after s.45 and s.47.
@ref s.41(b), s.45, s.47 (src:366-367, src:374-375)
GIVEN violation IS A Violation
      `the number of months for which the violation continued` IS A NUMBER
      `the violation is a repeat violation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the amount is updated` IS A DATE
      `the year of the first update day` IS A NUMBER
      `the index readings` IS A LIST OF `Price index reading`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation, held to the cap of s 41(b)` violation `the number of months for which the violation continued` `the violation is a repeat violation` `the day on which the amount is updated` `the year of the first update day` `the index readings` MEANS
    min (`s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation` violation `the number of months for which the violation continued` `the violation is a repeat violation` `the day on which the amount is updated` `the year of the first update day` `the index readings`) (`s 41(b) — the cap on a column B amount for` (violation's `the violator`'s `kind of person`))

-- The floor of s.46(a) (fork F-FLOOR): "the amounts fixed under this subchapter".  s.45 is in the subchapter, so the amounts
-- include the additions (taken); the alternative counts only the column B amount as updated.
@ref s.46(a) (src:370)
GIVEN violation IS A Violation
      `the number of months for which the violation continued` IS A NUMBER
      `the violation is a repeat violation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the amount is updated` IS A DATE
      `the year of the first update day` IS A NUMBER
      `the index readings` IS A LIST OF `Price index reading`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 46(a) — the amounts fixed under the subchapter for the violation, additions included` violation `the number of months for which the violation continued` `the violation is a repeat violation` `the day on which the amount is updated` `the year of the first update day` `the index readings` MEANS
    `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation` violation `the number of months for which the violation continued` `the violation is a repeat violation` `the day on which the amount is updated` `the year of the first update day` `the index readings`

@ref s.46(a) (src:370)
GIVEN violation IS A Violation
      `the day on which the amount is updated` IS A DATE
      `the year of the first update day` IS A NUMBER
      `the index readings` IS A LIST OF `Price index reading`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 46(a) — the amounts fixed under the subchapter for the violation, column B only, as updated` violation `the day on which the amount is updated` `the year of the first update day` `the index readings` MEANS
    `s 47(b) — the amount of` (`s 41(a) — the amount the Third Schedule fixes for the violation` violation) `updated on` `the day on which the amount is updated` `, the first update being in` `the year of the first update day` `and the index readings being` `the index readings`

-- The update day itself (kind R, a recurring date outside IL s.10): 1 January, even when it is a day of rest (taken).  The
-- alternative moves it past days of rest, recess or holiday as IL s.10(c) would (fork F-R).
@ref s.47(b) (src:375)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 47(b) — the update day of` year `if s 10(c) moved it past days of rest, with` calendar MEANS
    `s 10(c) — the last day of a period whose nominal last day is` (YMD year 1 1) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`Chapter 6 — the days of rest, recess or holiday of` calendar)

§§§ `s 47(c): the Commissioner publishes the updated amounts in Reshumot`

-- src:376 | {{ח:תת|(ג)}} הממונה יפרסם ברשומות הודעה על סכומי העיצום הכספי המעודכנים לפי סעיף קטן (ב).
-- No time is stated, so no WITHIN.  The Law does not say that the update waits for the publication (F-PUBLISH
-- in the open questions): the duty is encoded as independent of the update.
@ref s.47(c) (src:376)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under ss 45 to 47`
`s 47(c) — the Commissioner must publish the updated amounts in Reshumot` MEANS
    PARTY `the Commissioner`
    MUST  `publish in Reshumot a notice of the updated amounts of the financial sanction` `the Commissioner`
    HENCE FULFILLED
